{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "090J", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:531fa67d053fb15e054b94d5ef26dd969836eba8d8415a11826ac394ee0eecc1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>weakly contractible<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> object of a site is one that satisfies\nthe equivalent conditions of the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9ad3fae955a771a10580c45f14e3c6307546f5b0ebbc452a9e37de069011ce21", "unit_id": "tag:090J:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "090J", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0005": "$h_U^\\# \\to \\coprod h_{U_i}^\\#$", "MATH_0006": "$\\coprod h_{U_i} \\to h_U$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{G}(U)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-w-contractible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5619c592b46a5e5fbb006359e3ac37b18cbb2ad995917717d10f3b81b888dcac", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ef710cc9b6fbea6e96d081b9e7d4406fe2d3dfa60b43f89799f6eb48584dab7f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nThe following conditions are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> For every covering <MATH_0004> there exists a map of\nsheaves <MATH_0005> right inverse to the sheafification\nof <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every surjection of sheaves of sets <MATH_0007>\nthe map <MATH_0008> is surjective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2249d744cdcb7a8c44a5ead816a0506ab496efd1eb2e007955edd2c2d8d5931c", "unit_id": "tag:090K:statement"}
