surjective\n(Lemma <REF_0003>).\nHence by (2) there exists a section <MATH_0014> of <MATH_0015> mapping\nto the section <MATH_0016> of <MATH_0017>. This section corresponds to a map\n<MATH_0018> which is right inverse to the sheafification\nof <MATH_0019> which proves (1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:335df901f2b8b3b9d95230b194a30ad0b2e61d84b5ea796d6d64a59e56b77219", "unit_id": "tag:090K:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "090J", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$U_i$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$P$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$P$", "MATH_0013": "$U$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$U_i$", "MATH_0017": "$P$", "MATH_0018": "$i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-w-contractible}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-w-contractible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:82be644fca68a0941cdd44bdbc48479c2d70a3fd24edea28a5121a8acdab7052", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d891bdc5616ead9389bdab7fad3259d76f749e2e597766644d45389f52308b03", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say an object <MATH_0002> of <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>weakly contractible<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif the equivalent conditions of Lemma <REF_0001> hold.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say a site has <TEXTITOPEN_0002>enough weakly contractible objects<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif every object <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> has a covering <MATH_0006>\nwith <MATH_0007> weakly contractible for all <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0004> More generally, if <MATH_0009> is a property of objects of <MATH_0010>\nwe say that <MATH_0011> has <TEXTITOPEN_0003>enough <MATH_0012> objects<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if every object <MATH_0013> of\n<MATH_0014> has a covering <MATH_0015> such that <MATH_0016> has <MATH_0017>\nfor all <MATH_0018>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:08bb7dfcebe21a969a3896aeccc8347af5cbcc68747937cf39f9a4689f296a88", "unit_id": "tag:090L:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "090J", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{A}^1_\\mathbf{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a132cd5bdb243765faaf70717eb8f8715db9fadc224df104049d0ee8e1cb70e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2f8861db463ac27a71f33ce66de34c61b0d186cf2f07d072bcd6355a3fd63aaa", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe small <ACCENT_0001>tale site of <MATH_0001> does not have\nany weakly contractible objects. On the other hand, the small\npro-<ACCENT_0002>tale site of any scheme has enough contractible objects.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b129bbd8305c28490b4b6ddd8da13582d92948f0167a2a9b2b3e3eeb35a7f4fb", "unit_id": "tag:090J:prose-0002"}
